[71.524173, "o", "\r\n=== Page 1 ===\r\nTemporally multiplexed ion-photon quantum interface via fast ion-chain transport\r\nBingran You,1,2 Qiming Wu,1,2,∗ David Miron,1,2 Wenjun Ke,1\r\nInder Monga,2 Erhan Saglamyurek,1,2 and Hartmut Haeffner1,2,†\r\n1Department of Physics, University of California, Berkeley, CA 94270, USA\r\n2Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory, Berkeley, CA 94720, USA\r\n(Dated: January 12, 2026)\r\nHigh-rate remote entanglement between photon and matter-based qubits is essential for dis-\r\ntributed quantum information processing. A key technique to increase the modest entangling rates\r\nof existing long-distance quantum networking approaches is multiplexing. Here, we demonstrate\r\na temporally multiplexed ion-photon interface via rapid transport of a chain of nine calcium ions\r\nacross 74µm within 86µs. The non-classical nature of the multiplexed photons is verified by mea-\r\nsuringthesecond-ordercorrelationfunctionwithanaveragevalueofg(2)(0)=0.060(13),indicating\r\nnegligible crosstalk between the multiplexed modes. In addition, we characterize the motional\r\ndegree-of-freedomoftheioncrystalaftertransportandfindthatitiscoherentlyexcitedtoasmuch\r\nas n¯ ≈ 110 for the center-of-mass mode. Our proof-of-principle implementation paves the way\r\nα\r\nforlarge-scalequantumnetworkingwithtrappedions,buthighlightssomechallengesthatmustbe\r\novercome.\r\nRemoteentanglementacrossdistantquantumnodes[? light at convenient wavelengths for quantum frequency\r\n? ] maybeusedforlong-distancequantumkeydistribu- conversion (QFC) [? ? ], and the possibility of long-\r\ntion [? ? ], modular quantum computer architectures [? lived storage of entanglement [? ? ]. On the other hand,\r\n? ], as well as quantum enhanced metrology and sens- implementing a multiplexed light-matter interface with\r\ning [? ? ? ]. Light-matter quantum interfaces are a fun- these systems is technically challenging. Towards over-\r\ndamental building block for such applications, and allow coming this problem, a few multiplexing schemes have\r\nfor distributed entanglement between stationary matter already been proposed for ion and atom-based quantum\r\nqubits by using \"flying\" photons. processors [? ? ? ? ]. The only reported experimental\r\nFor practical purposes, these quantum interfaces need work, we are aware of, is the demonstration of multi-\r\nto be capable of establishing remote entanglement at plexing using a static three-ion chain [? ]. In view of the\r\nhighratesacrossalarge-scalenetworkofquantumnodes. recentadvancesofthequantumCCDarchitecture[? ? ?\r\nHowever, in widely adopted probabilistic schemes based ], a complementary approach to multiplexing is the pro-\r\non heralded photon detection [? ? ? ], it is infeasible to cess of ion-transport through a specific spatial location\r\ndistribute entanglement at useful rates over a few kilo- with maximized photon coupling efficiency.\r\nmeters, as the attempt rate is limited by the round-trip\r\nIn this work, we demonstrate a temporal multiplexing\r\ntravel-timeofphotonsinasinglemode. Forexample,for\r\nschemebasedonthetransportofanion-chainforimprov-\r\n"]
[71.524234, "o", "a communication distance of 10km, photon-travel time\r\ning the rate of ion-photon entanglement over long dis-\r\nwill be around 100µs, meaning that the attempt can-\r\ntances. In our experiments, we generate on-demand sin-\r\nnot be higher than 10kHz. In this scenario, even with\r\nglephotonsbyshuttlinganine-ionchainacrossthefocus\r\nuseofastate-of-the-artphoton-matterinterfacethatcan\r\nofasingle-ionaddressingbeam. Thisschemeisexpected\r\nyield close to unity photon extraction efficiency [? ], the\r\nto lead to a nearly nine-fold increase in attempt rate of\r\nmatter-photonentanglementratebeyondtensofkilome-\r\ntheentanglementgenerationforquantumrepeaternodes\r\nterswouldbelimitedtosub10s−1 withtotallossaround\r\nseparated by >100 km. We verify the single-photon na-\r\n15dBafterconsideringthecollectiveprobabilityofgener-\r\nture of the photon trains by measuring a second-order\r\nating and detecting telecom photons at each node, along\r\ntime correlation of g(2)(0) = 0.060(13) without back-\r\nwith the optical fiber loss [? ? ].\r\nground subtraction. Furthermore, we address the prob-\r\nA key solution to this challenge is multiplexing: to lem of motional excitation during the transport, which\r\ncombine multiple signals into a singlechannel and there- is detrimental to local entangling operations [? ] and\r\nfore increase the attempt rate [? ? ]. Multiplexing has in the case of using a cavity for stimulating the photons\r\nbecome a mature technology for ensemble-based quan- would lead to uncertainly in the coupling strength. [?\r\ntum interfaces, both in atomic gases and rare-earth ion ]. Using a shuttling function designed to mitigate mo-\r\ndoped solid-state systems [? ? ? ? ]. However, large- tional excitation, we find coherent excitation of n¯ ∼ 50\r\nα\r\nscalelocalquantuminformationprocessingistechnically on the center-of-mass (COM) mode during one round of\r\nchallenging in these platforms [? ]. ion chain transport. These results show tha