[190.679047, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.679113, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[190.683609, "o", "             a temporally multiplexed ion-photon interface via rapid transport of a chain of nine calcium ions"]
[190.683878, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.683986, "o", "             across 74 µm within 86 µs. The non-classical nature of the multiplexed photons is verified by mea-"]
[190.68411, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.684232, "o", "             suring the second-order correlation function with an average value of g (2) (0) \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K=\u001b[m\u001b[K 0.060(13), indicating"]
[190.684361, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.684451, "o", "             negligible crosstalk between the multiplexed modes. In addition, we characterize the motional"]
[190.684589, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.684691, "o", "             degree-of-freedom of the ion crystal after transport and find that it is coherently excited to as much"]
[190.684816, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.684947, "o", "\u001b[36m\u001b[K--\u001b[m\u001b[K"]
[190.685075, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.685185, "o", "ters would be limited to sub 10 s−1 with total loss around        separated by >100 km. We verify the single-photon na-"]
[190.685322, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.685418, "o", "15 dB after considering the collective probability of gener-      ture of the photon trains by measuring a second-order"]
[190.685517, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.685612, "o", "ating and detecting telecom photons at each node, along           time correlation of g (2) (0) \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K=\u001b[m\u001b[K 0.060(13) without back-"]
[190.685726, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.685814, "o", "with the optical fiber loss [? ? ].                               ground subtraction. Furthermore, we address the prob-"]
[190.685926, "o", "\r\n"]
[190.686016, "o", "   A key solution to this challenge is multiplexing: to           lem of motional excitation during the transport, which"]
[190.686122, "o", "\r\n"]
